  "nameStory": "",
  "description": "The Grey Knight (Tricholoma terreum) is a small to medium-sized mushroom characterized by its distinctive grey cap and white to pale gills. It is a terrestrial fungus belonging to the Tricholomataceae family, commonly found in coniferous and mixed forests throughout New England.",
  "idTips": [
    {
      "label": "Cap Color",
      "description": "Grey to dark grey conical or bell-shaped cap with a silvery or radially fibrous appearance",
      "isPrimary": true
    },
    {
      "label": "Gills and Stem",
      "description": "White to pale grey gills that are free or nearly free from the stem, with a white to pale grey cylindrical stem",
      "isPrimary": false
    },
    {
      "label": "Odor and Taste",
      "description": "Mild, pleasant odor resembling new-mown hay or flour, with a mild taste",
      "isPrimary": false
    }
  ],
  "habitat": "The Grey Knight thrives in coniferous and mixed forests, particularly near spruce, fir, and pine trees, preferring moist acidic soils in New England woodlands.",
  "seasonality": {
    "spring": "",
    "summer": "",
    "fall": "",
    "winter": ""
  },
  "funFact": "Despite its edible reputation in some regions, the Grey Knight is often avoided by foragers due to the difficulty in distinguishing it from toxic lookalikes, making proper identification essential before consumption.",
